  "status": "published",
  "title": "Concrete Planter Trio",
  "summary": "Three planters cast between pairs of nested plastic tubs, each with a drain hole. Learn to mix and cure concrete on something small.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 5,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Pair the tubs into three sets where the inner tub leaves at least a 1 in gap on the sides and bottom, and spray every surface the concrete will touch with release spray.",
    "Cut a 1 1/2 in piece of PVC pipe for each planter and stand it in the centre of the outer tub's bottom to form the drain hole.",
    "Wearing gloves and a dust mask, mix the topping mix with water in the mixing tub until it holds together like thick oatmeal.",
    "Fill each outer tub 1 in deep, press the inner tub down onto it, weigh the inner tub with gravel, and fill the walls in layers.",
    "Tap the sides with the rubber mallet all the way round to bring air bubbles up, and smooth the top rim with the trowel.",
    "Cover the planters with plastic and keep them damp for three days before demoulding, then sand the rims with a diamond pad.",
    "Let them cure another week, then brush on two coats of concrete sealer before planting."
  ],
